module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DeRham.LogPoles.LocalEquation
public import StacksFrontier.LinearAlgebra.ExteriorPower.KoszulSplitting

/-!
# The splitting of the differential forms along a local equation

Let `A → B → R` be a tower of commutative rings and let `R'` be a quotient of `R` as a
`B`-algebra whose kernel is generated by a single nonzerodivisor `t`, the local equation. Under
the smoothness hypotheses of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DeRham.LogPoles.LocalEquation` the map `g ↦ g · dt` is a split
injection `R → Ω[R⁄A]`, so

`Ω[R⁄A] = R · dt ⊕ M`

for a complement `M`, and the exterior powers split accordingly,

`⋀^{p+1} Ω[R⁄A] = ⋀^{p+1} M ⊕ dt ∧ ⋀^p M`.

This is the decomposition that the de Rham complex of log poles is built from: it is the
displayed computation at the start of the proof of Stacks Tag 0FMW, which reads
`Ω^p_{X/S, y} = ∧^{p-1}(M) df ⊕ ∧^p(M)`, in the local-ring form in which the geometric statement
meets it.

## Main results

* `Stacks.LogPoles.exists_isCompl_ker_contraction_range_wedgeLeft_D`: **the splitting**, that
  there is a functional on `Ω[R⁄A]` taking the value `1` on `dt` for which, in every degree, the
  kernel of the Koszul contraction and the range of wedging with `dt` are complementary in
  `⋀^{p+1} Ω[R⁄A]`.

## Implementation notes

The complement `M` is not canonical — the source says "`Ω_{X/S, y} = 𝒪_{X, y} df ⊕ M` for some
module `M`" — and accordingly the statement is existential in the splitting functional rather
than in possession of a distinguished `M`. The existence is exactly
`Stacks.LogPoles.exists_linearMap_apply_D_eq_one`, and nothing is chosen here: the functional is
bound by the existential, and the splitting is then the general
`exteriorPower.isCompl_ker_contraction_range_wedgeLeft` applied to it, which is constructive in
the functional.

Both summands are described intrinsically, by a kernel and a range, rather than by exhibiting
`M = ker φ` and its exterior powers inside `⋀ Ω[R⁄A]`; see the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier.LinearAlgebra.ExteriorPower.KoszulSplitting` for why.

The second condition of Tag 0FMV, that `⋀^p Ω[R⁄A]` is `t`-torsion free, is not needed for the
splitting and is not assumed here; it is
`Stacks.LogPoles.isSMulRegular_exteriorPower_kaehlerDifferential`, proved under the same
hypotheses, and is what the inclusion into the forms with a pole along the divisor needs.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FMW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FMW), whose proof opens with
  this decomposition
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FMV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FMV), the hypothesis under
  which it holds
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

universe u

namespace Stacks.LogPoles

section Tower

variable {A B R R' : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [CommRing R] [CommRing R']
  [Algebra A B] [Algebra B R] [Algebra A R] [IsScalarTower A B R]
  [Algebra B R'] [Algebra R R'] [IsScalarTower B R R']

/-- **The exterior powers of `Ω[R⁄A]` split along a local equation.** If the kernel of `R ⟶ R'`
is generated by the nonzerodivisor `t` and the smoothness hypotheses of
`Stacks.LogPoles.exists_linearMap_apply_D_eq_one` hold, then there is an `R`-linear functional
on `Ω[R⁄A]` taking the value `1` on `dt` whose Koszul contraction splits every exterior power:
in degree `p + 1` the kernel of the contraction and the range of wedge multiplication by `dt`
are complementary. Writing `M` for the kernel of the functional this is
`⋀^{p+1} Ω[R⁄A] = ⋀^{p+1} M ⊕ dt ∧ ⋀^p M`, the decomposition opening the proof of Tag 0FMW. -/
theorem exists_isCompl_ker_contraction_range_wedgeLeft_D [IsLocalRing R] [Nontrivial R']
    [Algebra.FormallySmooth B R] [Algebra.FormallySmooth B R']
    {t : R} (ht : t ∈ nonZeroDivisors R) (hsurj : Function.Surjective (algebraMap R R'))
    (hker : RingHom.ker (algebraMap R R') = Ideal.span {t}) :
    ∃ φ : Ω[R⁄A] →ₗ[R] R, φ (KaehlerDifferential.D A R t) = 1 ∧
      ∀ p : ℕ, IsCompl (LinearMap.ker (exteriorPower.contraction φ p))
        (LinearMap.range
          (exteriorPower.wedgeLeft (R := R) (KaehlerDifferential.D A R t) p)) := by
  obtain ⟨φ, hφ⟩ :=
    exists_linearMap_apply_D_eq_one (A := A) (B := B) (R' := R') ht hsurj hker
  exact ⟨φ, hφ, fun p ↦
    exteriorPower.isCompl_ker_contraction_range_wedgeLeft φ _ hφ p⟩

end Tower

end Stacks.LogPoles

end
